config FORTISOC_BASE_CONTAINER
	string "FortiGate base container (local path, optional)"
	depends on TARGET_fortisoc
	default ""
	help
	  By default, the TFTP image the boot loader runs from RAM (boot menu
	  option [R]) is built around a synthetic firmware container that
	  holds no vendor bytes.

	  As a fallback, give here the path to a base container extracted by
	  the user from a firmware image of his own appliance: the kernel is
	  then put in its ext2 instead. That container is proprietary: an
	  image built from it must not be distributed.
